- **Byte-level encoding:** iterating `s.utf8` means a character like é (two UTF-8 bytes) becomes %C3%A9 — two escapes — which is what RFC 3986 requires; iterating Characters and escaping code points would produce the wrong bytes.
- **Space as %20:** space (0x20) is simply not in the unreserved set, so it falls into the escape branch — the `+` convention belongs to form encoding (application/x-www-form-urlencoded), which the spec explicitly doesn't use.
- **Order and duplicates:** the builder maps over the array as given — no dictionary anywhere — so [("tag", "a"), ("tag", "b")] survives as tag=a&tag=b, and callers keep control of ordering.
- **Worked check:** [("q", "a b&c"), ("lang", "")] gives "q=a%20b%26c&lang=" — the & inside the value is escaped to %26 so it can't be mistaken for a pair separator.

